Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.459 align:start position:0%
 
I think it's one of the most gutless  vindictive and petty things I've ever  seen in English sport Kevin Pietersen  was directly told by Andrew Strauss his  incoming boss Colin grades ECB chairman  that if you want to get back in the  England team he had to go back to a  County and play county cricket and score  runs that's exactly what he's done he's  up the scored runs he's currently  averaging over 200 he scored three  hundred and fifty five not out in his  recent innings which ended this morning  he's in the form of his life according  to him and yet Andrew Strauss has shut  the door  that was opened by Andrews Frances boss  so understandably Kevin Peterson feels  extremely letdown betrayed and I believe  he thinks he's been lied to  you've spoken to him today I have spoken  to him throughout this process and he  told me three or four days ago that  Andrew Strauss and Tom Harrison the new  ECB boss under Colin Gray's wanted to  see him and we both agreed it could only  be for one reason and that would be to  rubber-stamp the previous bat because  Andrew Strauss has made no secret of his  hatred of Kevin Pietersen lot and all he  stands for but the bottom line is Kevin  Peterson gave up a very lucrative IPL  Indian Premier League contract to come  back to Surrey and play for nothing all  his salary is going to his crooked  Foundation which is a charity and he's  done that because the the boss of the  ECB said to him if you do that the score  runs you're back in the running for the  England being low batting lineup well  what more could he have done  he's just scored one of the highest  scores in the history of cricket and yet  the first reaction of Andrew Strauss was  to say you will not be playing this  summer I think most reasonably minded  cricket fans in this country will share  his sense of outrage Strauss says  there's still a question of trust there  is a trust issue because he tweeted a  gangster and texted against his England  colleagues when he was playing for  England and of course subsequently he  wrote that autobiography which made it  pretty clear what he thought of a lot of  his colleagues  well all these cricketers write books  Graham Swan wrote a very contentious  boat and carried on playing for England  for years our - it's under Andrew  Strauss so one rule for him one rule for  Kevin Pietersen Kevin Peterson's book  was a direct response to the tissue of  lies that the ECB deliberately leaked to  favor journalists the months after he  was sacked to try and justify what  they'd done  we were told with a dossier of 50  misdemeanors the Kevin had committed in  Australia not one of them has actually  been borne out by any substance or fact  the were no misdemeanors there is no  reason why he was sacked other than  certain people and that team were  jealous of him and didn't like the cut  of his jib well frankly if that is a  reason to not play professional sport  what England would have half a team in  almost any of the sports that we have  national teams in but do you think his  colleagues in the team could play with  him or trust them I think most of the  young players in the team love Kevin  Peterson if you took Jo route aside or  into a balance aside you too Bella side  you take some of the others in Australia  like Carberry they all talk very highly  about Kevin Peterson the problem has  only ever been with a small clique of  players the senior level led by broad  and prior and others and let's not  forget that Trust is a two-way street  some of that team last year or year and  a half ago started a bogus Twitter  account which ridiculed and mocked Kevin  Peterson on an almost hourly basis so  when it comes to trust this is not just  a question of Kevin Peterson it's a  question of the other players on the  team who were vindictively going after  him - and Andrew Strauss knows that but  has chosen to ignore that some of the  perpetrators like Stuart Broad are still  in the England team so there seems to be  one rule for him and one rule for  everybody else and Kevin Peterson at the  end of the day remains England's best  and most explosive batsman as we have  seen in the last 24 hours with this  incredible innings most of the best  sportsman in the world that come out  today after Andrew Strauss his statement  and said what on earth is going on this  is down to bad management Kevin Peterson  should not be dropped the England team  because Andrew Strauss doesn't like it  it should be dropped because he's not  good enough and nobody thinks he's not  good enough  you think Peterson has changed has his  as he grown up a bit as his character  changed as he become more amenable to  being a team player as a result of  what's happened to him in recent months  well this whole mythology about him not  being a team player Kevin Peterson was  part of the most successful team that  England cricket has ever had a retain  year period but what is being a team  player me when Manchester United won the  treble in 1999 two of their main  strikers Teddy sharing when Andy Cole  didn't exchange a single civil word to  each other in the entire season  who cares frankly if they're all happy  campers singing love songs to each other  in the dressing room I couldn't give a  monkey's I want them to score runs and  beat the Australians this summer and we  have a better chance of beating them  with Kevin Pietersen them without him  now has he changed I think he's got a  bit older I think he's got a bit more  mature  I think he's accepted some of the things  he did perhaps you know rubbed people up  the wrong way but he hasn't fallen out  of nightclubs drunk he doesn't take  drugs he's a great father he's a great  husband he's the hardest trainer in the  team and nobody can test that he's ever  done anything on the pitch to bring the  England shirt into disgrace or ignominy  and so the question remains what has he  done that's so bad that means he can't  play for his country other than annoy  Andrew Strauss  I mean his critics are saying that their  other English batsmen who are scoring  centuries and therefore it's crowded at  the top well why don't we ask the  Australian fast bowlers who they would  least like to see coming in in the  middle order for England this summer and  the number one person they would least  like to see is the guy but let's not  forget was the top scorer in the last  Ashes series and that's Kevin Peterson  he was the top scorer and then got  sacked I felt at the time that was  utterly ridiculous  I remain of that view English cricket  has collapsed since Kevin Pietersen left  the team after 10 glorious years of  success and frankly it's time that the  petty vindictive egos of the English  cricket ball were put to one side and  the interest of the England team the  country and the fans that pay these guys  wages were put first DAWs Peterson or  indeed do you think there's any chance  that he will make it into the test team  this summer  I think there's zero chance of Kevin  Pietersen making the team if Angie  Strauss is in charge with this blinkered  bigoted view of him so my solution would  be if we lose against New Zealand which  we might easily do in a couple of weeks  time and we lose the first couple of  tests against Australia which we might  easily do I would fire and just try and  bring back Kevin Pietersen because this  is personal  it's not about cricket it's not about  Peterson's ability even Straus admits  he's a fantastic batsman but the idea  that a man can score 355 runs and then  be taken into a room by Andrew Strauss  and told you're not playing the summer  for England is utterly ridiculous Piers  Morgan thank you for joining us

